5. **`totals_for`.** Change the signature to `async fn totals_for(app: &App, patch: Option<&str>, drills: bool)` and set `patch: patch.map(str::to_string),` in the query. Change the doc's first line to "R1044000: one patch's totals (every patch's with `None`) over both sources and every mode, each card's turn and co-played". In `kept_report`, change the call to `totals_for(app, Some(patch), with_drills)`. Nothing else in `kept_report` changes.

6. **`KeptHistory`.** After `kept_report` (before `get_cards`'s doc comment), add:
   ```rust
   /// R2491000: one `?pilot=` and `?mode=`'s patch history, which every card's drill-down reads: each
   /// shipped patch whose live games clear R654's gate, in `patches.json`'s order, with each card's
   /// in-deck tally there as `patch_report` counts it.
   struct KeptHistory {
       patches: Vec<(String, IndexMap<String, Tally>)>,
   }

   type KeptHistoryCell = Arc<OnceCell<Arc<KeptHistory>>>;
   ```
   Only the in-deck tallies are kept, not whole `CardStatsReport`s, so the memory stays small. Record this decision too.

7. **`kept_history`.** Directly below, add the following. Copy the `compute` / `get_or_try_init` pattern of `kept_report`:
   ```rust
   /// R2491000: the patch history of `versions` for `pilot` and `mode`, as kept: read off every
   /// patch's totals in one load when none was made in the last `CARD_STATS_CACHE_TTL_SECONDS`, once
   /// however many requests miss it together, each version cut from it by `patch_report` as its own
   /// load was (R978000), so the figures are the same.
   async fn kept_history(
       app: &App,
       versions: &[String],
       pilot: PublicStatsPilot,
       mode: PublicStatsMode,
   ) -> Result<Arc<KeptHistory>, ApiError> {
       let compute = || async move {
           let totals = totals_for(app, None, false).await?;
           let patches = versions
               .iter()
               .filter_map(|version| {
                   let kept = patch_report(
                       &totals,
                       version,
                       SourceParam::Default,
                       pilot.filter(),
                       mode.filter(),
                       false,
                   );
                   (kept.live_games >= PUBLIC_STATS_MIN_LIVE_GAMES).then(|| {
                       let cards: IndexMap<String, Tally> = kept
                           .report
                           .cards
                           .into_iter()
                           .map(|stat| (stat.card, stat.in_deck))
                           .collect();
                       (version.clone(), cards)
                   })
               })
               .collect();
           Ok::<_, ApiError>(Arc::new(KeptHistory { patches }))
       };
       let cell = app.card_stats.history_cell((pilot, mode), now_ms());
       let kept = cell.get_or_try_init(compute).await?;
       Ok(Arc::clone(kept))
   }
   ```
   This gives the same figures because `card_stats_of` and `StatsTotals::live_games` both filter by `patch`, and the tallies are integers sorted by card id. So `patch_report` over the all-patch load gives each version exactly what it gave over that version's own load.

8. **`get_card`.** Replace the comment `// R978000: each patch's history and the current patch's drill-down read the kept reports.`, the `let mut patch_history …` line and the whole `for version in &versions { … }` loop with:
