## Tests

In `crates/server/tests/api/stats.rs`, add this module (step 10):

```rust
mod r2491000_kept_card_history {
    use super::*;
    use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicUsize, Ordering};

    use jackioh_server::api::catalog::load_patch_versions;
    use jackioh_server::db::store::{Db, StoreError};

    /// Counts the fake store's `statsTotals.load` calls from here on, through its `on_call` hook.
    async fn count_loads(app: &App) -> Arc<AtomicUsize> {
        let loads = Arc::new(AtomicUsize::new(0));
        let counter = Arc::clone(&loads);
        match &app.db {
            Db::Fake(data) => {
                data.lock().await.on_call = Some(Arc::new(move |method: &str| -> Result<(), StoreError> {
                    if method == "statsTotals.load" {
                        counter.fetch_add(1, Ordering::SeqCst);
                    }
                    Ok(())
                }));
            }
            Db::Pg(_) => panic!("the API tests run on the fake store"),
        }
        loads
    }

    /// The loads one request to `path` made, which answers 200; the count starts again after it.
    async fn loads_of(app: &Arc<App>, loads: &AtomicUsize, path: &str) -> usize {
        let (status, _, _) = get_public(app, path).await;
        assert_eq!(status, 200, "{path}");
        loads.swap(0, Ordering::SeqCst)
    }

    /// A live game of `mode` on `patch` whose first seat, on `core-001` and `core-002`, `winner` wins.
    fn game(id: String, patch: &str, mode: &'static str, winner: &'static str) -> Value {
        make_game_record(
            &id,
            RecordOptions {
                source: Some("live"),
                mode: Some(mode),
                patch: Some(patch.to_string()),
                p1_deck: Some(vec!["core-001", "core-002"]),
                winner: Some(winner),
                ..RecordOptions::default()
            },
        )
    }
    // the two tests below
}
```

The module holds two tests, both `#[tokio::test(start_paused = true)]`:

- **`r2491000_a_drill_down_reads_its_patch_history_in_one_load_kept_per_match_type`.** Set up `test_app()`, then `let loads = count_loads(&app).await;`, then `assert!(load_patch_versions().await.len() > 2);`. For each of `"/api/stats/cards/core-001"`, `"…/core-001?mode=bo1"`, `"…?mode=bo3"` and `"…?mode=random"`, assert `loads_of(&app, &loads, path).await == 2` (pass `path` as the message). Then assert `0` for `"/api/stats/cards/core-001"` again and `0` for `"/api/stats/cards/core-002?mode=bo3"`. Before the change the first four make one load per patch and the fifth makes 79.
- **`r2491000_the_kept_history_lists_each_cleared_patch_as_its_own_load_did`.**
  - Set up: `gate = count(PUBLIC_STATS_MIN_LIVE_GAMES)`, `current = current_patch()`, `versions = load_patch_versions().await`. Let `past` be `versions.iter().filter(|v| **v != current)`, `old = past.next()…clone()` and `short = past.next()…clone()`.
  - Insert, in one `insert_records`: `gate` games `game(format!("hist-old-{i}"), &old, "bo1", "p1")`, one game `game("hist-short-0".to_string(), &short, "bo1", "p1")`, and `gate` games `game(format!("hist-now-{i}"), &current, "bo3", "p2")`.
  - Define `let row = |patch: &str, games: usize, rate: Value| json!({ "patch": patch, "games": games, "winRate": rate });`.
  - Assert `/api/stats/cards/core-001`'s `["patches"] == json!([row(&old, gate, json!(1.0)), row(&current, gate, json!(0.0))])`. `short` is below the gate and absent.
  - Assert `?mode=bo1`'s `== json!([row(&old, gate, json!(1.0)), row(&current, 0, Value::Null)])`. The gate counts every mode.
  - Assert `/api/stats/cards/core-005`'s `== json!([row(&old, 0, Value::Null), row(&current, 0, Value::Null)])`.

